{"id":10,"date":"2016-05-16T12:50:26","date_gmt":"2016-05-16T12:50:26","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/masterbadminton.dev\/all-england-badminton-2012-home-advantage-not-enough-for-top-english-pairs\/"},"modified":"2016-08-31T17:46:11","modified_gmt":"2016-08-31T17:46:11","slug":"all-england-2012-quarter-finals-news-html","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/all-england-2012-quarter-finals-news.html","title":{"rendered":"All England Badminton 2012: Home Advantage Not Enough for Top English Pairs"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"ContentColumn\">\n<div class=\"Liner\">\n<div style=\"float: left;\"><\/div>\n<p>It was a tough day for English badminton fans. 2 of the best English mixed doubles pair; Chris Adcock and Imogen Bankier; Nathan Robertson and Jenny Wallwork, have been eliminated.<\/p>\n<p>With the support from the home crowd, both pairs fought hard in 3 games. But both failed to exploit the home ground advantage.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Chris Adcock and Imogen Bankier<\/strong> lost to Chan Peng Soon and Goh Liu Ying of Malaysia (21-16, 15-21, 21-17).<\/p>\n<p><strong>Nathan Robertson and Jenny Wallwork<\/strong> (ENG) were shown the exit by Indonesians Tontowi Ahmad and Liliyana Natsir (21-19, 14-21, 21-6).<\/p>\n<p>Here&#8217;s an interview with Robertson and Jenny after their quarter final match.<\/p>\n<div align=\"center\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/0RG8TY_ZNHQ\" width=\"420\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"><\/iframe><\/div>\n<h2>Outstanding Performance by Malaysia&#8217;s Chan Peng Soon &amp;amp Goh Liu Ying<\/h2>\n<p>It was a thrilling match between Chris Adcock &amp;amp Imogen Bankier (ENG) and Chan Peng Soon &amp;amp Goh Liu Ying of Malaysia.<\/p>\n<p>It was the second encounter between the 2 sides with the Malaysians winning the previous encounter. Despite that, the English pair achieved second place at the 2011 Badminton World Championships.<\/p>\n<p>The English crowd were behind their home players all the way, but this was not enough.<\/p>\n<p>Chan Peng Soon was just in an incredible form. The 23 year old Malaysian covered the centre and rear court excellently.<\/p>\n<p>The Malaysians have been playing extremely well this year.<\/p>\n<p>They reached the semi-finals on their home ground, in the Malaysian Super Series early this year.<\/p>\n<p>Now, they&#8217;ve successfully won another opportunity to play in the semi-finals of this All-England Super Series Premier.<\/p>\n<p>Let&#8217;s watch a post match interview with these young Malaysian pair.<\/p>\n<div align=\"center\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/ObMiem5bQ_M\" width=\"420\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"><\/iframe><\/div>\n<h2>Taufik Gave It All in First Set against Lin Dan<\/h2>\n<p>It was a clash between badminton&#8217;s top players. Former Olympic champion, Taufik Hidayat current Olympic champion, Lin Dan met in the quarter finals.<\/p>\n<p>Taufik put up a good fight in his first set against Lin Dan.<\/p>\n<p>Lin Dan had to work very hard to win every point in the rallies. Taufik&#8217;s performance lately has not been that outstanding.<\/p>\n<p>But this time, his performance in this All-England quarter final shows that our former World and Olympic Champion is back!<\/p>\n<p>Unfortunately, at 31 years of age, Taufik could not keep up with the game. Super Dan eventually took a wide lead in the 2nd match. It finished 21-18, 21-8.<\/p>\n<h2>Mathias Boe\/Carsten Mogensen (DEN) Wants another Title<\/h2>\n<p>Top Danish men&#8217;s doubles pair Mathias Boe and Carsten Mogensen successfully eliminated their rivals, Chai Biao and Guo Zheng Dong (21-12, 21-19). It&#8217;s never an easy task seeing off Chinese opponents.<\/p>\n<p>Defending champions Boe\/Mogensen are definitely looking to make their way to the All-England finals. The previous All-England finalists Koo Kien Keat\/ Tan Boon Heong were eliminated.<\/p>\n<p>However, competition will still be tough as world no.2 Jung Jae Sung\/ Lee Yong Dae will be meeting them in the semi-finals!<\/p>\n<p>If they manage to get through, their opponents will most likely be the current world champions, Cai Yun\/ Fu Hai Feng of China.<\/p>\n<div class=\"retnvbx1\"><\/div>\n<div class=\"fb-comments-intro-ns\">\n<div class=\"retnvbx\"><\/div>\n<h3><span class=\"teelmeww\">Tell me what you think!<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>What do you think about what you just read? Leave me a comment below.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div id=\"COMMENTING\" class=\"fb-comment\">\n<div class=\"fb-comments\" data-href=\"http:\/\/www.how-to-play-badminton.com\/all-england-2012-quarter-finals-news.html\" data-num-posts=\"15\" data-width=\"100%\"><\/div>\n<h3 class=\"fblikeste\">Like Masterbadminton.com?<\/h3>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<div id=\"fb-root\"><\/div>\n<p><script><![CDATA[\n(function(d,s,id){var js,fjs=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];if(d.getElementById(id)){return;}js=d.createElement(s);js.id=id;js.src=\"..\/connect.facebook.net\/en_US\/all.js#xfbml=1\";fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js,fjs);}(document,'script','facebook-jssdk'));\n><\/script>\n\n\n<div align=\"left\"><\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n\n<div align=\"center\"><\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>It was a tough day for English badminton fans. 2 of the best English mixed doubles pair; Chris Adcock and Imogen Bankier; Nathan Robertson and Jenny Wallwork, have been eliminated. With the support from the home crowd, both pairs fought hard in 3 games. But both failed to exploit the home ground advantage. Chris Adcock [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[22],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-10","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-badminton-news"],"yoast_head":"<!-- Th